<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Blambangan Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1300 CE – 1768 CE (approx.) · capital Panarukan (later Macan Putih)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Hindu kingdom of Java, on the island's eastern tip, which held out against Muslim Mataram until conquered by the Dutch in 1768.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blambangan">Blambangan</a> emerged in the eastern salient of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> as a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>, and after Majapahit's decline in the 15th and 16th centuries it became an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> kingdom, with its early capital near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panarukan">Panarukan</a>. Javanese legend remembers its ruler Menak Jingga as the enemy in the Damarwulan story.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blambangan">Blambangan</a> was a sparsely populated realm of forests and small ports, caught between Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>. It fought repeated wars with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram Sultanate</a> and often accepted Balinese protection, especially from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-buleleng">Buleleng</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-mengwi">Mengwi</a>. In the 17th century Prabu Tawang Alun founded a new capital at Macan Putih.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a> invaded in 1767 to 1768 to keep out the British, and suppressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puputan-bayu">Puputan Bayu</a> rising of 1771 to 1772 with heavy loss of life. The region became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banyuwangi">Banyuwangi</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osing-people">Osing people</a> preserve a distinct language and culture.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/blambangan-kingdom.jpg" alt="Blambangan Kingdom" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: JongjavaV1 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Blambangan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1300 CE – 1768 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Panarukan (later Macan Putih)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tawang Alun</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Javanese (Osing)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Balambangan, Blambangan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1534&amp;focus=blambangan-kingdom" aria-label="Blambangan Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7832 2465 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Blambangan Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8152 2721L8112 2721M8152 2721L8182 2753M8152 2721L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8112 2721h0M8182 2753h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8152 2721h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8152 2721h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Panarukan. <a href="/atlas?year=1534&amp;focus=blambangan-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

